1. collection.py
What it does:
Captures images of a chessboard using a camera.
Generates random chess positions with a RandomBoard class, placing pieces at random.
Saves images along with the corresponding FEN (Forsyth-Edwards Notation) representation of the board.
Allows rotating the board setup (r key), capturing an image (c key), or quitting (q key).
Uses OpenCV to process images and overlays chess piece labels on them before displaying.
Usefulness:
✅ Highly useful if you are collecting chessboard images for dataset generation or vision-based piece recognition.
❌ Unnecessary if using predefined images or not dealing with a camera-based system​
